title A floor that refuses every rise
prompt the standing autonomous lap -- reds first, then the lane's next crux
rota lap 4204, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; the concrete fact before the argument about it. Its threshold asks what already stands true at the door, and that is exactly how the lap turned: the cold roster printed `plant red 1s` with `control_verdict=ok` and `faults=0` on the lines directly above it, and reading those three lines whole rather than reasoning about them named the fault in one step. The helper was perfect. Only the census had moved.
think Opened the round out of order and said so: I ran the cold roster before `fleet_round_open.sh`, so the pass measured a tree one commit behind `xy`. The pass still earned its finding, and the tree was clean, so the open cost nothing beyond a stale receipt.
think The cold pass answered `guards_red=2`. `standing_equipment` reds because it reads the receipts the same pass recorded, so the two are one root: `plant`.
think `plant_witness.rish` asserts `adoption.out contains "sourcing=13"`. The live scan reads 14. A peer had adopted the plant law in a control since the number was last edited by hand.
think The assertion sits beneath its own comment naming it "a floor that only rises" and under a header calling adoption "reported rather than gated". Neither describes an equality, which refuses a rise exactly as hard as a fall. The tree's own law reads: a guard that reds on ordinary work is a guard someone turns off -- and here the ordinary work is the adoption the guard exists to encourage.
think The witness header records the number being hand-raised seven times in one day: 4, 5, 7, 9, 11, 12, 13. Every one of those edits was a lane paying a fleet-wide refusal for doing the right thing. That is a lantern that has fired eight times, so it is a loom.
think %578 repaired this same instrument eleven hours earlier -- the MEASURING half, where a grep for a path read a comment as an import. It left the comparison that reads the measurement. Two halves of one instrument, repaired a day apart, because only the measuring half was where anybody looked.
think Put the number in one place: FLOOR=13 as a constant in the scan, compared `sourcing >= FLOOR`, reported as `adoption_floor_held=` and refused by name as `verdict=adoption_regressed`. The balance check is asked first, since a reading that does not sum has measured something other than adoption.
think The control's new pen is a real git repository, because the scan reads `git ls-files` -- the index, never the working tree -- so a pen of loose files would read zero controls and every leg would pass for the wrong reason.
think The floor is moved either side of the pen's count by `plant_apply`, which is this control's own subject. A control proving the plant law with a plant is the honest shape, and a stale plant then reads `nothing` rather than passing quietly.
think The load-bearing leg strips the refusal block out of a copy and watches the same below-floor pen walk free at verdict=ok. A floor that has merely started saying yes passes every welcome leg.
think Second half of the lap: %574 stood OPEN because petrichor declined to widen the grader's Reach reading, naming the reason honestly -- it re-grades every page unmeasured. That is a measurement, not a ruling, and measuring is agent-doable.
think Ran both readings side by side from a copy in /tmp, changing nothing in the tree: the elder `/^[ \t]*[-*>#]/` against the register scan's four rules plus its front-matter block.
obs The floor repair closes two rostered guards with one change, since standing_equipment was reading plant's own receipt.
obs %574 measured: over 120 front doors the widened Reach moves 83, mean +3.66 composite, minimum -10, maximum +25, and ZERO fall below B while 15 rise to it. The only gate that exists -- card_below_b at a ceiling of 0 over the 13-page door roster -- holds under both readings, with no page crossing downward.
obs A 140-page Field sample of foundations, rules and context moves 25 pages, mean -0.04, one falling across B and one rising. So the re-grade is bounded, roughly neutral at Field, and upward at the doors.
obs The durable shape for %574 is one file both readings call, the way reference_block.awk already is called rather than copied. The card LIFTS measure() verbatim so Register cannot drift and then spells Reach's filter a second time, which is the whole of the red.
obs I did not land that change. It is a peer's open row with a question standing at Keaton, and what it lacked was a number rather than a hand. The number is on the card now.
obs Two questions dropped off my card block to stay under its bound, both one click away on the shelf: the %499 park-or-rebase question, which COPAL's block still asks in full, and the mycelium Door-negatives reading.
